    {
     "id": "1da70d9d-e3b7-5daf-808f-a4f7a0db825b",
     "title": "Article 2 ",
     "description": "<div>\r\n\tThe text of Article (<a href='/legislations/7d3f2340-8b44-4946-b7bc-2a573a223471?almawadId=cb254012-8f31-4dac-b4cd-54cb34780538'>2</a>) of <a href='/legislations/7d3f2340-8b44-4946-b7bc-2a573a223471'>Decision of the Minister of Labour and Social Affairs No. (4) of 2015</a> referred to above is replaced with the following text:\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\t&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\t<u><strong>Article (2):</strong></u>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\t&laquo; Employers are required to transfer the wages of employees hired on an annual or monthly wage to the employee's account in financial institutions within the State, within seven days from the date such wages are due, through the Wage Protection System (WPS). The wage of the employee is due on the first day of every Gregorian month.&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\tAs for the wages of other employees, they are due on the first day of every two weeks.&raquo;\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\t&nbsp;\r\n</div>",
     "footerNote": "",
     "oldTitle": "",
     "oldDescription": null,
